# Trivy findings accepted for the image gate (platform LLD §12; testing.md §2; C38).
# Format, enforced by scripts/ci/images.sh (one finding per line):
#   <CVE-or-GHSA-id> # reason: <why it is acceptable>; owner: <github handle>; exp:YYYY-MM-DD
# Every entry is also recorded in SECURITY_DEPENDENCIES.md. Trivy stops honouring an entry after
# its exp: date, and the policy check fails on it, so an acceptance is always re-reviewed.
# Accepted 2026-11-10 (S9); reviewed 2026-11-11 (C78), when the web image moved to Debian 13 like the
# Python images: Debian 13 base-image packages with no fixed version (status affected or
# fix_deferred); the fixable findings are removed in the Dockerfiles instead.
CVE-2025-69720 # reason: no Debian fix yet: terminal library of the base image, unused by a non-interactive server; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-119373 # reason: no Debian 13 fix yet: the Python services never import sqlite3, and the web never uses node:sqlite (Node bundles its own SQLite), and neither uses FTS5 or session changesets; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-119374 # reason: no Debian 13 fix yet: the Python services never import sqlite3, and the web never uses node:sqlite (Node bundles its own SQLite), and neither uses FTS5 or session changesets; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-119379 # reason: no Debian 13 fix yet: the Python services never import sqlite3, and the web never uses node:sqlite (Node bundles its own SQLite), and neither uses FTS5 or session changesets; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-16742 # reason: no Debian fix yet: systemd-homed is not present or run in the container, only the client libraries are installed; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-54369 # reason: no Debian fix yet: libacl is not used by the services, which run non-root on a read-only root filesystem; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-76642 # reason: no Debian fix yet: mount and nsenter tools need privileges the pods drop (non-root, no capabilities) and are never run; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-78408 # reason: no Debian fix yet: mount and nsenter tools need privileges the pods drop (non-root, no capabilities) and are never run; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-78409 # reason: no Debian fix yet: mount and nsenter tools need privileges the pods drop (non-root, no capabilities) and are never run; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-78410 # reason: no Debian fix yet: mount and nsenter tools need privileges the pods drop (non-root, no capabilities) and are never run; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-9538 # reason: Debian fix deferred: perl Archive::Tar is never run in the containers; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
